# One-off data-migration artefacts (Daraz cover/soldCount backfills,
# merchandising flag snapshots). Written to the repo root by scripts in
# backend/scripts as a rollback safety net — useful locally, but they are
# point-in-time dumps of catalogue state, not source, and they bloat clones.
# The existing ones stay on disk; they are simply no longer tracked.
daraz-*-backup-*.csv
merchandising-flags-backup-*.json
reprice-backup-*.json
# Catalogue/backlog reports, same reasoning: generated by backend/scripts,
# useful locally, superseded on every run.
backlog-*.csv
orphaned-live-books.csv

# Misc
*.pem
.cache/
.turbo/

# OS crash dumps
*.stackdump
